 "relevance_note": "The paper describes one identifiable LCAT patient (Case 2): 'A 64-year-old male ... Genetic testing identified a missense variation [NM_000229.2(LCAT):c.349G > A, p.Ala117Thr ...] in the LCAT gene'.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; JSON assembled with a short Python script from hand-chosen values and spans. Three cases are described (ABCA1 Tangier family incl. an affected sister, LCAT, APOA1); only the LCAT patient (Case 2) is in scope; the ABCA1 and APOA1 patients and the Tangier sister get no rows (cohort_size_as_stated = 3). Label 'Case 2' is the paper's own section label. Table 1 has patients as columns; the column header for this patient is 'LCAT mutation' (data column 2). Lab-based features (low HDL, hypertriglyceridemia, low apoA1) are judged by comparing the patient's value with the table's 'Normal values range' column, so spans quote the whole row; no units are printed. Total cholesterol 88 (80–200), LDL 62 (no range), apoB 56 (40–125) and the two rows both labelled 'Apolipoprotein C2' (7; 17.9) were not turned into features; 'low ldl cholesterol or apolipoprotein b' left not reported. Atherosclerotic disease is taken only from the Discussion group statement 'Early-onset atherogenic disease was a common feature across all three cases'; Case 2's own text mentions no atherosclerotic event. Contradictions: (1) variant type: Case 2 text says 'missense variation' but the Figure 1D legend says 'homozygous splice site error at position 349 substituting G to A'; missense recorded from the text. (2) Zygosity 'homozygous' comes only from the Figure 1D legend; the Case 2 text does not state zygosity. (3) Summary says 'three patients with mutations in CETP, LCAT, and ABCA1' whereas the cases are ABCA1, LCAT and APOA1. Pathogenicity and 'reduced enzyme activity' are cited from ref 15, not measured in this paper. is_proband set true as the single patient of the Case 2 report (not called proband). n_patients_reported = 1 is the single LCAT case among the three; the authors do not state '1' explicitly.",
